# File: sudoers-smart-locker
# Description: Grants the Smart Locker service account passwordless sudo for the
#              EXACT privileged commands the in-app Software Update, Stop system,
#              and Shut down buttons need — managing its own systemd service,
#              launching the transient update unit, and poweroff — and nothing else.
# Project: smart_locker/deploy
# Notes: apply-sudoers.sh (called from install.sh and update.sh) renders this
#        to /etc/sudoers.d/smart-locker with __APP_USER__ and __APP_DIR__
#        substituted, mode 0440, owned by root, and validates it with
#        `visudo -cf`. Every command is fully specified (no trailing
#        wildcard). The update.sh path must stay root-owned and not writable
#        by __APP_USER__ (install.sh / update.sh keep the tree root-owned;
#        only logs, photos, backups, and the SQLite files are service-writable).
#        Keep LF line endings.
__APP_USER__ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl start smart-locker.service, /usr/bin/systemctl stop smart-locker.service, /usr/bin/systemctl restart smart-locker.service, /usr/bin/systemctl start smart-locker, /usr/bin/systemctl stop smart-locker, /usr/bin/systemctl restart smart-locker, /usr/bin/systemd-run --collect --unit=smart-locker-update /bin/bash __APP_DIR__/deploy/install/update.sh
__APP_USER__ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl poweroff
